{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '6589,6614p;10195,10210p;10274,10310p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md | sed -n '94,125p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '140,148p'\"","aggregated_output":"  6589\t## D543 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the cold reflection on the lean path: D518 stands with its reasons, the choice of system is not made in Alex's place, and no investigation is opened (reflection council consensus)\n  6590\t\n  6591\t- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-2/`): Claude's own reflection written first\n  6592\t  (`own-reflection.md`); a fresh independent Codex session reading the whole record cold (`handoff-cold.md`, `cold-codex-1.md`);\n  6593\t  one challenge round (`cold-challenge-1.md`, `cold-codex-2.md`). Both readings, made apart, reached the same place.\n  6594\t- **Why the path did not reach its goal (agreed):** the fresh week mixed a difference of product policy with a comparison of\n  6595\t  quality (three of the old system's four covered matters are questions Alex's rule forbids the new system, D505); the evidence\n  6596\t  was too thin to rank answers (one run a system, seven answers against fifteen, readers' bars apart); the work followed each\n  6597\t  newly exposed defect instead of asking whether resolving it would select a system (the dependency stretch is the clearest\n  6598\t  case); and the council often corrected work already framed on a premise that the stored request, an earlier decision or the\n  6599\t  order of events contradicted.\n  6600\t- **Conclusions marked as weaker than they look:** \"no eligible judgement disagrees\" in the July comparison (few were eligible);\n  6601\t  \"36 of 438\" (repeated daily readings on a few question paths, not an error rate); the three unsupported answers with a\n  6602\t  missing stored figure (two matters, cause not shown); the new system's three confirmed missing pairs (a minimum; the one test\n  6603\t  was inconclusive); the dependency connection (a conditional replay; it also removes seven filing links).\n  6604\t- **Decided, citing D439:** D518 stands, restated with its reasons: the old system stays the default and both systems stay,\n  6605\t  for continuity and because the new system's answer-choice step has not passed its tests and it is not integrated with\n  6606\t  production storage. The quality of the two systems' answers is not ranked and **the choice of a foundation is not made in\n  6607\t  Alex's place** (the reviewer withdrew \"carry the old system forward provisionally\" as readable for such a choice). No\n  6608\t  investigation is opened: no bounded test on the record is likely to change the choice at a justified cost, and no narrow\n  6609\t  defect is reopened to postpone it. The two problems that do not depend on the choice stay recorded: related facts reaching\n  6610\t  the question that needs them (no common cause or tested general fix among the known cases), and the judge's amounts with\n  6611\t  nothing sizing them (what the product shows is Alex's choice). The pages were corrected where a cold reader could be misled\n  6612\t  (the advice's reasons; \"the one test that could decide\"; a stale \"waiting on Alex\" and an unsourced spend figure on the\n  6613\t  status page; \"three small mismatches\"; \"36 of 438\" without its qualification). A new step worth a decision returns to the\n  6614\t  council under D439.\n 10195\t  - the whole-window replay waits until a candidate clears the screen;\n 10196\t  - card C100 (M08) is to be rechecked independently; the recorded score stands until then.\n 10197\t- Spend: phase 1 $2.4 of $3, and the separating test $0.28 of the $2 `phase1b` ledger.\n 10198\t\n 10199\t## D684 · 2026-11-20 · Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the iteration to Claude (\"那你自己持续迭代\")\n 10200\t\n 10201\t- **Alex, 2026-11-20**, in reply to the request for approval of council H's one test: \"那你自己持续迭代\".\n 10202\t- **Decided:**\n 10203\t  - the presentation-only test runs on fresh cases, as council H wrote it;\n 10204\t  - Claude continues the phase-1 loop on its own: council before every send, a council round on every result, every trace read by\n 10205\t    Claude, every round logged. The limits of D439 stand: the frozen ruler and the frozen production files never change, nothing is\n 10206\t    pushed, deployed or committed unasked, credentials and caps are untouched, and paid spend stays inside D439's $40;\n 10207\t  - D382 (company-figure questions in the hybrid) stays open for Alex; the judge's phase does not depend on it.\n 10208\t- **The fresh pool, written before any reading** (`fresh_test.py pool`, `DESIGN-J2.md`, \"The fresh test\"): each question's latest\n 10209\t  judgement on or before 2026-09-06 in the 5 draws, excluding the 73 question-and-draw pairs whose answers the design read. 116 answers,\n 10210\t  all rebuilt byte for byte under the frozen judge.\n 10274\t## D688 · 2026-11-20 · Under D687 (council M): no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone; to Alex, keep old and pause the hybrid's release line\n 10275\t\n 10276\t- **Council M** (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-m-*`; Codex thread 01a1f7a7, memories off):\n 10277\t  - round 1: CONSENSUS on deferring any release test, with corrections;\n 10278\t  - round 2: DISAGREE, reclassifying M27 and recommending option 2;\n 10279\t  - round 3: CONSENSUS, with one wording change, taken here.\n 10280\t- **The attainable check, $0** (`OPENING-CENSUS.md`, last two sections).\n 10281\t  - Old's per-draw served counts: 3 of 3 for M11, M13, M15, M18 and M31; 2 of 3 for M04 (counting 1), M06, M10, M17 and M19; 1 of\n 10282\t    3 for M05, M09 and M25, and for M30 under counting 2.\n 10283\t  - Noise alone costs an estimated 1.4 of the 2-of-3 matters.\n 10284\t  - Within D687 and Alex's standing rules, the concrete opening misses are M20 and M05:\n 10285\t    - M20: a $125B unsigned obligation that old folds into the total in 3 of 3 draws, against D388/D389;\n 10286\t    - M05: a theme quantity refused once under a free name.\n 10287\t  - M09, M30 and M25 are coin flips.\n 10288\t  - Not misses under the rules:\n 10289\t    - M12: a signed deal under a plan tracked by amount (D248 boundary 1, D388);\n 10290\t    - M27: separately answerable in principle, but its public settlement source is unproven;\n 10291\t    - M07: a distinct segment forecast, but the evidence does not establish a missed opening;\n 10292\t    - M16: allowed by the standard, but its wording lever failed in D481 and leaves the ceiling until a different mechanism has\n 10293\t      evidence behind it.\n 10294\t  - What binds: the list counts finer than D248/D388 on 9 matters, the library's NVIDIA-only subject on 5, and D198 for the judge's 2.\n 10295\t- **Decided (council, Claude agreeing):**\n 10296\t  - The census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone. Five gains with zero losses would pass on paper,\n 10297\t    but only M20 and M05 are concrete, and the noise losses are an estimate.\n 10298\t  - No opening test and no M20 account probe are sent for release.\n 10299\t  - The release bar stays.\n 10300\t- **To Alex, one recommendation:**\n 10301\t  - Keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. The judge and reading fixes remain quality work.\n 10302\t  - Questions on key figures of other research-list companies are offered only if he wants those forecasts for their own value.\n 10303\t  - D543 applies, since another test would leave the decision unchanged.\n 10304\t- **Errors of mine, both corrected before council M closed:**\n 10305\t  - the first attainable check counted M12, M27 and M16 as gains within the rules without reading D248 boundary 1, D388 and D481;\n 10306\t  - the census section listed the categories without the decisions that bound them (AGENTS §2.4).\n    94\t## What this decides, and what it does not\n    95\t- **Decided:** wiring c8 under the old questions delivers the matters' decisive statements to the judge, with no five-company or 2027\n    96\t  figure taken as the answer. Both readers support the hybrid answers on M04 and M17, as they support old's. The registered test still\n    97\t  did not pass: P2's proxy clause and V missed.\n    98\t- **Not decided:**\n    99\t  - whether the merge serves *more* matters: the new-only matters need the clean opener;\n   100\t  - Steps 2–3 grouping;\n   101\t  - the other 30 matters;\n   102\t  - cost.\n   103\t- **Cost, priced from tokens.** The merge pays the old pipeline plus c8 reading: about $0.0125 per article at $1.75 / 140. Over the\n   104\t  82-day window's 1,884 articles that is about $24 on top of old's about $9.\n   105\t- **The sampler-sensitive v47 question needs more than one draw** before stability is claimed.\n   106\t\n   107\t## Where the old system loses on the 32 matters, and why this merge cannot raise its score ($0, read after the verdict)\n   108\tSources: the comparison's `reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/mapping.json` and `deck/readings.json`, and the deck key.\n   109\t- **Old serves 10 and never opens 17.** The 17 are M01–M03, M07, M12, M16, M20–M24, M26–M29 and M32 (only new-3 opened M32). The merge\n   110\t  keeps old's opening, so these stay lost.\n   111\t- **Opened in at least 2 of 3 old draws but not served: M08, M14 and M30.**\n   112\t  - Every M08 and M14 answer was rejected by the readers. The readers' reasons are judge reasoning, not missing material:\n   113\t    - M14 (four companies' 2027 capex): rung 4 was taken from NVIDIA's own $1.3T forecast or a five-company $1.08T total. In old-1 the\n   114\t      material held BofA's four-company $930–980B.\n   115\t    - M08 (NVIDIA's outstanding investment commitments): $25B and $18B were added, though they probably overlap (old-2, old-3). In\n   116\t      old-1 the answer was anchored on Bank of America's $70B, a cumulative investment estimate rather than an outstanding balance.\n   117\t      (Corrected 2026-11-20. A first version cited \"a range against its own estimate of about $53B\". That card, C140, was a planted\n   118\t      reader control, not a system answer.)\n   119\t  - M30 is a company figure (D382/D505).\n   120\t- **Served in only 1 of 3 old draws:** M05, M09 and M25.\n   121\t- **The consequence.** Clean Step 1 reads more of the facts. The old system loses at opening and at the judge's reasoning, neither of\n   122\t  which better reading fixes. The test's targets, M04 and M17, were matters old already served, so the test could show \"does not\n   123\t  break\", never \"improves\". That was a design error of mine.\n   124\t- **Across all old cards rated worth tracking:** 18–21 of 28–29 supported per draw; 3–5 unsupported per draw.\n   125\t\n   140\t## Open defects\n   141\t\n   142\t1. **Competitor and customer news is filed under the company's revenue questions** instead of the share, capital-spending or custom-chip question it informs (D355; filing is otherwise about 85% right). Share facts are often not written at all, an extraction recall miss. The total-revenue question holds about a quarter of all links (D354).\n   143\t2. **One bet opened twice** about one encounter in five: the collision judge splits a seed question from an identical candidate on a fine detail (D354).\n   144\t3. **A question the standard rules out** (the lidar legislation) was proposed by the extraction and opened in one draw of three (D354).\n   145\t4. **A thesis opened from an article gets no dependency of its own**: the default Jev matching asks for none (`views/jev_matching.py`), although D51 has the matching call choose them; themes still reach every company thesis through the theme block (D191, D195). Found in the 2026-11-05 consolidation; building it is decided (D368).\n   146\t5. **Historical coverage-start reading, retired by D370** (D364–D366): the capital-spending line is missed in about one read in six (the question is then left as it was); a labelled guidance figure is written with the fact tier; later reports reach the questions only through the daily stream; `scripts/preflight.py` does not replay the reading's check.\n   147\t6. **Measured on one company and one 14-day window**, the judgement scored at the window end only; no version of the current pipeline has completed a longer window (a 60-day run of `poc-v108` was stopped at Alex's word after 2026-07-15, [log row 8](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)). The China-share question (v17) swings between draws (0 of 3 in the acceptance, 2 of 3 in its control, 1 of 3 in the frozen draws): two readers found the starting figures did not cause the acceptance's drop, and the byte-identical extraction request kept a \"share fell to zero\" sentence in two candidate draws and dropped it in two control draws. One acceptance draw judged nothing on v16; its cause is not established.\n   148\t7. **What a judgement reads grows with the window** (D358). Argument records (D201) were measured as the remedy on 2026-11-04 and not built: judging-v8 agreed 12 of 17 against 15 of 17, judging-v9's card added little at about half again the judging cost; their code was removed at Alex's request ([log rows 4–11](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
