{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**Keep poc-v118 in production, record the release pause, and close the judge and c8 experiments for now. Give Alex a closure note with no decision requested.**\n\n**(a) Fresh means a fresh question.** New evidence on a question that shaped the design can test whether a repair holds up over time. It cannot count toward the eight independent failures needed for a fresh test. Count each distinct question once across draws and exclude close variants, as Council I did. I verified the 213 and 310 later articles. At the historical rate, processing them would cost about $2.50 per draw before reader review, with no assurance that they yield enough new questions. I agree to drop the $0 count of repeated forecasts. It cannot tell us which forecasts were wrong. [Council I’s selection rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:397) · [Article archive](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/items-window.sqlite)\n\n**(b) Give Alex the result.** Bring him the D198 choice and price once there are eight eligible failures, matched controls, and a source-checked summary worth testing. I agree D368 belongs in its existing defect record. None of the 24 rejected answers was traced to it in this review. [D543](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6604) · [Open defect 4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:145)\n\n**(c) D689 needs three wording changes.**\n\n- Attribute option 1 to Alex and the experiment closures to Council N. Keep the approval and funding requirements explicit for any future paid test. Record **$39.65–$44.42** as the two accounting scenarios, with **$0 available for new sends**.\n- Call the proposed measure a **future test’s pass criteria**. To reopen c8, trace a decisive fact old missed, show c8 delivers it, and identify the final answer it could change. A paired test with the same judge and question would establish whether it actually helps.\n- Say M14 improved in **two of three old draws**. The four repairs were four test cases, including M14 twice. China share regressed in the separate test using the usual limited evidence. Say c8 **showed no improvement in the answers tested**. [Judge results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:280) · [Merge results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md:94)\n\nFor Alex, I’d lead with “按你选的第一个方案，线上继续用旧系统，混合系统暂停上线。两边仔细复核后，建议先把判答案和读文章的试验都停下来。” Then give the four-company spending example, the spending correction, and one sentence on what would reopen each experiment.\n\nCONSENSUS"}}
